Appendix C. Evolutionary Simulation Engine — Formal Model

C.1 Genotype and Phenotype

An institution is encoded as a genotype string over an alphabet of grammar tokens. The phenotype is the executable institution \mathcal{I} obtained by parsing the genotype with the Institutional Grammar DSL. The fitness of a genotype g is

F(g) = 1 - p_{\text{collapse}}(g),

where p_{\text{collapse}}(g) is the probability that \mathcal{I}(g) enters a forbidden state within a 50‑year simulation horizon, estimated by Monte Carlo runs.

C.2 Evolutionary Dynamics

The population of M genotypes evolves according to a Moran process with mutation:

1. At each step, select an individual i to reproduce with probability proportional to its fitness F(g_i).
2. Generate an offspring by copying g_i and applying point mutations with rate \mu.
3. Select an individual j uniformly at random to die; replace it with the offspring.

Theorem C.1 (Stationary distribution).
The Moran process on a finite genotype space is an irreducible, aperiodic Markov chain. Its unique stationary distribution \pi satisfies

\pi(g) \propto \prod_{h \neq g} \left( \frac{F(g)}{F(h)} \right)^{\!M} \cdot \nu(g),

where \nu(g) accounts for mutation bias. For small \mu, the distribution concentrates on genotypes of high fitness.

Proof sketch. Standard results from population genetics. The candidate must adapt the proof to the specific mutation operator defined by the Institutional Grammar (e.g. structural mutations that preserve well‑typedness). The mixing time can be bounded using coupling arguments. ∎

C.3 PAC Guarantees

To estimate p_{\text{collapse}}(g) to accuracy \varepsilon with confidence 1-\delta, we require N independent simulation runs. Hoeffding’s inequality gives

\Pr\left( |\hat{p} - p| > \varepsilon \right) \le 2 \exp(-2N\varepsilon^2).

Setting the right‑hand side to \delta yields

N \ge \frac{1}{2\varepsilon^2} \ln\frac{2}{\delta}.

A dissertation must report \hat{p} with its associated (\varepsilon,\delta) values and verify that the number of runs meets this bound. For the whole evolutionary run, a union bound over candidate genotypes or a more sophisticated empirical process bound may be required.

