Appendix D. Governance Sandbox — Protocols and Calibration

D.1 Detailed Phase A/B Protocol

Duration: 28 days (4 weeks), split equally into Phase A (frozen rules) and Phase B (iterative amendment).

Participant Cohort: 12–20 members of the Academy of Colonists program, compensated via a Governance Bounty.

Data Streams (continuous):

· Resource transactions (water, food, energy) logged via the Governance UI.
· Communication volume and sentiment (derived from anonymised text and audio).
· Voting records, sanction filings, and legislative outcomes.
· Psychological surveys (daily PANAS, weekly group cohesion scales).

Metrics:

· Institutional throughput: number of legislative cycles completed, average consensus time.
· Resource volatility: standard deviation of reserve levels.
· Conflict index: number of sanctions per capita, escalation events.
· Collapse precursors: any metric crossing a pre‑registered red‑line triggers the external Auditor’s review.

D.2 Tier‑2 Agent Calibration

The Tier‑2 cognitive agents are based on Cumulative Prospect Theory (CPT). In each decision situation observed in the sandbox, participants choose between a safe institutional option (compliance) and a risky exploit. We fit the CPT parameters (\alpha, \beta, \lambda, \gamma) via maximum likelihood estimation:

\hat{\theta} = \arg\max_{\theta} \sum_{t} \ln \Pr(\text{choice}_t \mid \text{state}_t; \theta),

where the probability is given by the CPT value function and probability weighting function. The fitted parameters are then used to update the Tier‑2 agent population in the master simulation. A Bayesian hierarchical model pools data across multiple sandbox runs while allowing individual‑level variation.

D.3 Validation Loop

After calibration, the simulation is re‑run with the updated Tier‑2 agents to predict the Phase A behaviour. The predicted distributions of key metrics are compared to the actual sandbox data using the Jensen–Shannon divergence. If the divergence exceeds a threshold, the candidate must refine the agent model or the institutional grammar and iterate. Only when the model consistently reproduces the observed behaviour across multiple cohorts does it earn the designation “sandbox‑calibrated.”

